--- instructions (stderr):

First-run instructions for installation e7lab (deploy/stack.yaml; see docs/INSTALL.md).
No secret values are printed here. Create each secret from a file or stdin you control.

1. On EVERY Swarm node: create the agent state directory and the volume base:
     install -d -m 0755 /var/lib/dbcm-agent /var/lib/dbcm/volumes
2. On a Swarm manager node, create the database secrets and the cluster network
   (labelled with the installation):
     for s in dbcm-e7lab-root-pw dbcm-e7lab-monitor-pw dbcm-e7lab-backup-pw; do
       head -c 24 /dev/urandom | base64 | tr -d '\n' | docker secret create --label dbcm.installation=e7lab "$s" -
     done
     docker network create --driver overlay --attachable --label dbcm.installation=e7lab dbcm-e7lab-net
3. Store this configuration as a Swarm config (configs are immutable; use a new name per change):
     docker config create dbcm-manager-config-1 <this file>
4. Deploy on a Swarm manager node, pinned to the node at 192.168.104.1:
     DBCM_MANAGER_NODE=<hostname of that node> DBCM_DOCKER_GID=$(stat -c %g /var/run/docker.sock) \
       DBCM_CONFIG_NAME=dbcm-manager-config-1 docker stack deploy -c deploy/stack.yaml dbcm
5. Read the one-time setup token from the service log (printed only while no administrator exists):
     docker service logs dbcm_manager 2>&1 | grep 'setup token'
   Then open http://localhost:8080 through your TLS reverse proxy (to 127.0.0.1:8080 on that node) and create the first administrator.
6. Register the Swarm in the UI with Docker endpoint unix:///var/run/docker.sock; agents enroll at https://192.168.104.1:7444.
(exit 0)
```

